        "math_academy_id": "q-352247",
        "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+5x-1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
        "worked_solution": "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $3$ | $-7$ | $5$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $\u2193$ | $3$ | $-4$ | $1$ |\n|  | $3$ | $-4$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+5x-1}{x-1}=3{x}^{2}-4x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+5x-1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(3{x}^{2}-4x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}{|}_{1}^{2}-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{2}+x{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}{|}_{1}^{2}-2{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{2}+x{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =[{2}^{3}-{1}^{3}]-2[{2}^{2}-{1}^{2}]+[2-1] \\\\  & =7\\cdot 1-2(3)+1 \\\\  & =7-6+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "actual_result": "Correct",
